# Anomaly -- what this repo tracks
#
# Only what is needed to build and distribute the app: the Tauri + Svelte app and
# the hook DLL's source. Everything else in this working tree is generated,
# per-user, or a research aside, and is listed below with the reason.
#
# Leading slashes are deliberate: an unanchored `tests/` would also swallow
# app/tests/, which is part of the app.

# ---- build output ----
app/node_modules/
app/build/
app/.svelte-kit/
app/src-tauri/target/
app/src-tauri/gen/
hook/bin/
hook/obj/
/build/
/dist/

# ---- per-user state: not the same on any two machines ----
# Every user builds their own vanilla game cache against their own install, so
# none of it is portable and none of it belongs in version control.
/backups/
/_vanilla/
_vanilla/
/conflicts.html
/report.json
*.log
tools/nms_classes.json

# ---- the Python cross-check and the research tools ----
# The Rust engine is the product; this is the older cross-check implementation
# plus the offline metadata extractor. Kept locally, not shipped.
/nmscheck.py
/nmscc/
/tests/
tools/*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---- third-party binaries and environments ----
# Version-locked to the game and not ours to redistribute. tools/THIRD-PARTY.md
# records what they are and under which licence, and is tracked.
tools/venv/
tools/*.exe
# Third-party binaries live under tools/ but are never tracked -- they are not
# ours to redistribute through this repo, and each is version-locked to either
# the game or its own upstream. tools/THIRD-PARTY.md records what a release
# bundles, under which licence, and how to obtain or substitute each one.
# Upstream licence texts ARE tracked, because we are obliged to ship them.
tools/sevenzip/*.exe
tools/sevenzip/*.dll
tools/nmslogger/*.dll

# ---- editor and OS noise ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- extracted game data and anything derived from it ----
# nms_item_ids.py unpacks vanilla tables and localisation files out of the paks to
# build the item database. Those are Hello Games' files, not ours to redistribute,
# and every user regenerates them against their own install anyway.
tools/_itemgen/
tools/nms_items.json
tools/nms_items_ids.txt
tools/nms_classes.json
